The environment menu's exit node, runner side: report it with the Pod's use.

A session whose repositories name a tailnet exit node sends all its internet
traffic through it, so while it's offline the session has no internet, and
the agent can't reach its model either. Each report now carries exit_node:
the Pod's Tailscale service (images/runner/tailscale/tailscale-service.sh)
writes what it did with it to /run/omnigent-tailscale.exit-node.json,
{"name": ...}, with "error" when Tailscale refused it, or {"names": [...]}
when the repositories name different ones. read_exit_node reads that file and
asks tailscaled's LocalAPI over its socket (status, peers=false) whether the
exit node is online: state connected, offline, off (the Pod doesn't use it,
such as after the agent switched it off), failed, conflict, or unknown when
tailscaled doesn't answer. Without the file, exit_node is null and the menu
has no row. Over the socket rather than `tailscale status`, so a report never
starts a process. Reading it never costs the report, whose answer carries
Keep running: a file it can't make sense of reads as no exit node.
Pairs with the server patch 0021-environment-exit-node.patch.
Applies after 0011-environment-menu.patch. Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d).

